WEBVTT

00:01.890 --> 00:05.770
<i>This world is filled with 
too many games to count,</i>

00:06.980 --> 00:11.260
<i>though the vast majority simply 
come and go in obscurity.</i>

00:12.630 --> 00:15.400
<i>The greatest of all games</i>

00:15.400 --> 00:20.730
<i>is the fully immersive VR game boasting 
over 30 million players worldwide—</i>

00:20.730 --> 00:25.320
<i></i>Shangri-La Frontier<i>, which rightly 
earns the title of "god-tier game"!</i>

00:26.800 --> 00:30.910
<i>One lover of trash games, Rakuro Hizutome,</i>

00:30.910 --> 00:34.160
<i>is trying out the god-tier 
game, </i>Shangri-La Frontier<i>!</i>

00:34.930 --> 00:39.620
<i>What adventures await him there?</i>

02:11.930 --> 02:16.290
Want to take out the unique monster, 
Wethermon the Tombguard,

02:16.290 --> 02:17.740
with just the three of us?

02:18.260 --> 02:20.270
It looks like, in two weeks,

02:20.700 --> 02:24.450
I'll be picking a fight with 
"Wethermon the Tombguard."

02:24.790 --> 02:28.810
It's looking like I'll have to leave 
you out of the party while I do...

02:29.600 --> 02:30.460
What's wrong?

02:30.460 --> 02:35.210
Picking a fight with <i>Wethermon</i>?!

02:36.950 --> 02:38.650
D-Da... Bo...

02:38.650 --> 02:43.220
Daboo... Bodadd...

02:43.220 --> 02:49.480
I've got to tell my daddy!

02:52.000 --> 02:55.610
<b>The Glimmer of Truth</b>

02:59.430 --> 03:02.450
Emul filled me in,

03:02.780 --> 03:05.720
but I'd like to hear it directly from you.

03:07.450 --> 03:12.370
You're picking a fight with that 
fool who's outlived his time?

03:14.380 --> 03:17.610
<i>"Outlived his time"? Wethermon?</i>

03:18.090 --> 03:19.220
<i>What does that mean?</i>

03:20.030 --> 03:21.220
<i>But for now...</i>

03:21.730 --> 03:24.140
<i>This event got sprung on me out of nowhere,</i>

03:24.650 --> 03:26.720
<i>and it's gotta be an important one.</i>

03:27.530 --> 03:31.010
<i>Roleplaying based on the 
world and its characters—</i>

03:29.660 --> 03:34.230
"Roleplaying"
 To play one's given role in the setting.

03:31.460 --> 03:34.230
<i>That's my best choice in this situation.</i>

03:34.760 --> 03:35.700
<i>Stay calm.</i>

03:36.260 --> 03:40.860
<i>If you play your cards right, 
you could get valuable info on Wethermon.</i>

03:41.290 --> 03:43.890
<i>You beat </i>Failia<i>, right?</i>

03:44.280 --> 03:45.360
<i>You can do this!</i>

03:46.730 --> 03:48.160
<i>Get Vash on your side, here.</i>

03:48.690 --> 03:51.290
<i>The keyword is "vorpal soul."</i>

03:51.520 --> 03:53.110
I don't think I need to tell you

03:53.680 --> 03:57.480
how weak you still are.

03:59.640 --> 04:01.050
You're right, of course.

04:02.250 --> 04:07.050
I'm not doing this because 
I know I can win, Aniki.

04:08.010 --> 04:09.190
What's that?

04:10.540 --> 04:13.830
I'll actually be playing a support role.

04:13.830 --> 04:16.310
A friend of mine will 
do most of the fighting.

04:20.140 --> 04:25.660
Are you aware, Aniki, what's happening 
with Wethermon the Tombguard now?

04:26.290 --> 04:27.450
Nah.

04:27.450 --> 04:31.160
Last I saw of him was some time ago.

04:31.500 --> 04:36.530
This friend of mine says a 
group of PKers—rather...

04:37.120 --> 04:41.170
a no-good band of killers is exploiting 
Wethermon to make themselves stronger.

04:41.400 --> 04:43.560
They're using him as a tool.

04:43.930 --> 04:48.810
Since... well, you get lots of 
experience just for encountering him.

04:52.890 --> 04:57.170
The mastermind of our upcoming raid 
is technically part of that band,

04:57.690 --> 05:01.820
but she truly wants to defeat 
Wethermon the Tombguard.

05:02.000 --> 05:04.530
She's gone to unthinkable lengths to do it.

05:04.890 --> 05:07.550
No matter what lengths you go to,

05:07.550 --> 05:11.950
if there's no chance of victory, 
it's still a reckless move.

05:12.660 --> 05:18.700
When did I say "vorpal soul" meant walking 
straight into the mouth of death?

05:19.320 --> 05:24.720
Not one of us would go into a 
fight with the intention to lose.

05:25.760 --> 05:28.490
But my friend is determined 
to beat Wethermon,

05:29.000 --> 05:32.220
and I and our other companion 
believe in her cause.

05:35.000 --> 05:36.650
"We only get one chance at this."

05:37.260 --> 05:39.480
"Win or lose, this is our last shot."

05:40.050 --> 05:43.360
Those are the words my friend 
came to me with, and so...

05:44.140 --> 05:47.490
I feel honor-bound to offer my aid.

05:50.260 --> 05:53.170
I realize I'm still weak and inexperienced,

05:53.170 --> 05:56.120
but I have two weeks to do what I can—

05:56.770 --> 05:59.110
To transform the brash arrogance 
of a cocky greenhorn

05:59.660 --> 06:03.250
into the grit of a contender 
who's challenging a champion.

06:15.900 --> 06:18.390
Honor-bound, eh?

06:20.630 --> 06:24.150
He's an awkward one, you see.

06:24.620 --> 06:26.400
<i>He's talking about Wethermon?</i>

06:26.820 --> 06:30.630
Serious to a fault, 
never knows when to let up...

06:30.630 --> 06:34.110
He lost his wife to a lousy little lie,

06:34.420 --> 06:38.410
and ended up with that undying body of his.

06:40.150 --> 06:44.940
He's a living corpse, 
unable to even put himself to rest.

06:45.700 --> 06:46.840
And so...

06:48.150 --> 06:52.800
Someone has to take him down and 
bring him that well-earned slumber.

06:56.030 --> 07:00.900
I made up my mind not to 
interfere with "them"...

07:01.590 --> 07:05.320
But if you insist on doing 
this, I won't stop you.

07:08.250 --> 07:10.950
My sweet daughter's made a request, as well.

07:12.850 --> 07:13.910
Come along.

07:14.740 --> 07:20.010
I'll lend you a bit of a hand after all.

07:31.830 --> 07:33.090
<i>A forge?</i>

07:33.280 --> 07:38.720
<b>Good Communication</b>

07:33.750 --> 07:36.740
I moved on to the next stage of the event!

07:36.740 --> 07:38.720
So far, so good, man!

07:39.050 --> 07:42.220
Hey, Bilac! You here?

07:42.670 --> 07:43.660
Yeah?

07:43.660 --> 07:45.270
Hey, Pops.

07:45.270 --> 07:46.730
How about that, eh?

07:47.040 --> 07:49.990
<b>Bilac</b>

07:47.460 --> 07:49.430
Ain't seen you here in a while.

07:50.260 --> 07:51.900
Bee! Big Sis!

07:51.900 --> 07:53.430
Heya, Emul.

07:53.430 --> 07:55.980
<i>Another of Emul's siblings?</i>

07:56.390 --> 07:59.680
<i>Did Vash father the entire 
population of Rabituza?</i>

07:59.990 --> 08:01.910
<i>Probably not... right?</i>

08:03.740 --> 08:06.670
You the guy Pops and Emul told me about?

08:06.670 --> 08:07.820
Hey.

08:07.820 --> 08:09.420
Sunraku-san is his name!

08:10.490 --> 08:13.930
Gotcha. You got an air about 
you kinda like Evelle.

08:14.180 --> 08:15.530
<i>"Evelle"?</i>

08:15.530 --> 08:17.560
<i>Another rabbit name drop?</i>

08:17.560 --> 08:19.430
<i>Please, don't spring any more on me!</i>

08:19.430 --> 08:23.820
Well, take out your vorpal weapons already.

08:26.240 --> 08:27.810
Aha.

08:28.120 --> 08:31.320
These blades see you as 
a good master, for sure.

08:32.160 --> 08:35.380
They've got a fine countenance, too.

08:35.880 --> 08:38.330
They'll do us just fine.

08:40.440 --> 08:43.210
Bilac. I'm gonna ascend these.

08:44.580 --> 08:46.950
"Ascend"? Make them better?

08:46.950 --> 08:48.650
The best they can be!

08:47.770 --> 08:49.840
<b>Ascend
<b>"Bring to Truth"</b></b>

08:49.840 --> 08:51.240
Hang on...

08:51.240 --> 08:53.490
You're gonna wield the hammer, Pops?

08:56.860 --> 08:59.890
It'd be boring to just sit back and watch

08:59.890 --> 09:03.560
while he challenges that fool 
who's outlived his time.

09:05.700 --> 09:06.890
Hey, there we go!

09:06.890 --> 09:08.770
I'll get the forge lit!

09:09.110 --> 09:12.770
Got any decent materials on you?

09:12.770 --> 09:18.050
Ah, you know... from opponents 
you struggled to beat?

09:18.050 --> 09:19.550
Struggled to beat?

09:20.060 --> 09:22.930
<i>{M}Lycagon's the toughest I've faced...</i>

09:22.930 --> 09:24.880
<i>Though that was "struggled, <i>got</i> beat"...</i>

09:25.240 --> 09:28.380
<i>And I sold the stuff I got 
from the Mud Digger...</i>

09:30.040 --> 09:32.740
I didn't exactly get it 
through my own efforts,

09:32.740 --> 09:35.380
but I've got a material from a 
monster that was pretty darn tough.

09:35.810 --> 09:37.050
Hand it over.

09:46.570 --> 09:49.060
The shell of a Quad Beetle, eh?

09:49.060 --> 09:53.280
It held up against 
Empire Bee attacks for ages.

09:53.280 --> 09:55.950
I figured it had to be a 
pretty excellent material.

09:57.470 --> 09:58.400
It'll do.

09:59.870 --> 10:02.500
Now, let's get started.

10:17.630 --> 10:20.620
You're a lucky guy, y'know that?

10:21.330 --> 10:26.010
Pops hasn't wielded the hammer for years.

10:26.010 --> 10:29.440
Is that true? Um... Bilac?

10:29.440 --> 10:33.870
My brother inherited the... 
kingship, you'd say? Of Rabituza.

10:34.260 --> 10:36.530
And I inherited his forge.

10:37.020 --> 10:39.400
I suppose I never told you, Sunraku-san!

10:39.400 --> 10:41.400
Dadd—er...

10:41.960 --> 10:44.160
The boss is a blacksmith!

10:44.160 --> 10:45.540
A blacksmith?

10:46.040 --> 10:48.910
And not just any blacksmith.

10:51.210 --> 10:54.490
He's a Master Craftsman—a label given to 
those who master the blacksmith's art—

10:54.060 --> 10:59.800
<b>Master Craftsman</b>

10:54.490 --> 10:59.800
and an Ancient Craftsman—one who can 
forge the lost weapons of the Divinity.

10:58.320 --> 10:59.800
<b>Ancient Craftsman</b>

11:00.480 --> 11:03.280
Combining the two masteries 
makes him a Divine Craftsman.

11:02.550 --> 11:10.310
<b>Divine Craftsman</b>

11:03.590 --> 11:07.190
The superlative forger, 
peerless in the world of smithery—

11:07.190 --> 11:10.330
That's our Pops.

11:16.340 --> 11:18.320
It's about to begin, Sunraku-san!

11:35.400 --> 11:36.460
<i>{M}The heck was that?</i>

11:38.440 --> 11:39.610
<i>Magic circles?</i>

11:39.960 --> 11:43.300
<i>With each strike, they rise, then 
draw back into the weapon...</i>

11:43.300 --> 11:45.270
To "ascend" a weapon

11:45.270 --> 11:49.560
means reading the memories and 
experiences it's acquired in its battles

11:50.190 --> 11:52.700
and coaxing it into a more appropriate form.

11:52.700 --> 11:57.980
In other words, his transcendent 
skill grants it its "true" form.

11:57.980 --> 11:59.740
It's "true" form?

11:59.740 --> 12:01.720
Weapons that bear the name "vorpal"

12:01.720 --> 12:04.170
remember the battles they've 
fought against strong foes.

12:04.510 --> 12:07.200
The memories you've forged with 'em

12:07.410 --> 12:10.430
and the power of the strong 
foe you handed Pops earlier...

12:10.430 --> 12:12.640
He mixes 'em together in the forging process

12:12.640 --> 12:14.460
and changes the weapon's shape.

12:15.250 --> 12:17.920
And since you managed to 
mix it up with Lycagon,

12:17.920 --> 12:21.470
I'm <i>real</i> curious to see what 
your weapons will turn into.

12:26.200 --> 12:35.100
<i>The fire of the forge 
against the sleeping sky...</i>

12:36.010 --> 12:37.510
Is he singing—

12:43.110 --> 12:47.230
<i>Off fly the sparks</i>

12:47.230 --> 12:52.120
<i>Engulfed by the night</i>

12:52.120 --> 12:56.150
<i>The hammer dances</i>

12:56.150 --> 12:59.990
<i>The iron sings</i>

13:01.000 --> 13:05.320
<i>Bang, clang, ring</i>

13:05.320 --> 13:08.710
<i>Crash, clash, bash</i>

13:08.710 --> 13:13.260
<i>A blade's what you are</i>

13:13.260 --> 13:17.830
<i>Power's what you are</i>

13:26.530 --> 13:30.530
<i>Draw forth from the ground</i>

13:30.530 --> 13:32.590
<i>Feed in the wood</i>

13:32.590 --> 13:36.540
<i>Stoke the flame</i>

13:36.540 --> 13:40.540
<i>Temper the metal</i>

13:40.540 --> 13:44.300
<i>Cool it in water</i>

13:44.300 --> 13:48.540
<i>The world turns</i>

13:48.540 --> 13:52.990
<i>And then it stops</i>

13:52.990 --> 13:57.690
<i>From metal comes iron</i>

13:57.690 --> 14:01.960
<i>From iron comes steel</i>

14:01.960 --> 14:07.210
<i>From steel comes a blade</i>

14:07.210 --> 14:12.080
<i>From blade comes a sword</i>

14:28.800 --> 14:33.250
<i>Dawn breaks in the night sky</i>

14:33.250 --> 14:37.490
<i>The sword glimmers</i>

14:37.490 --> 14:41.930
<i>It reflects the light</i>

14:41.930 --> 14:46.410
<i>It tears through the dark</i>

14:46.410 --> 14:50.890
<i>As the sword dances,</i>

14:50.890 --> 14:55.740
<i>let the world sing</i>

15:25.300 --> 15:26.690
All right.

15:27.450 --> 15:32.200
The Vorpal Chopper has taken 
its true name and form.

15:32.200 --> 15:33.700
Its name...

15:34.250 --> 15:38.440
Moonblade (Waxing)
and Moonblade (Waning).

15:36.640 --> 15:38.440
<b>Moonblade (Waxing) 
</b>A twinblade with a crescent-shaped blade.

15:36.640 --> 15:38.440
<b>Moonblade (Waning)
</b>A twinblade with a crescent-shaped blade.

15:38.440 --> 15:39.940
A twin weapon?!

15:40.330 --> 15:42.330
One blade in the form of two.

15:42.620 --> 15:47.200
Each needs the other to have meaning.

15:47.880 --> 15:51.340
It's been a while since I saw 
one change form, you know?

15:52.540 --> 15:54.840
Let's check this baby out!

15:55.270 --> 15:56.940
"Waxing—

15:56.940 --> 16:00.050
when fighting an opponent of higher level,

16:00.050 --> 16:06.730
successful criticals reduce your HP, but a 
power bonus is added to your next attack."

16:06.080 --> 16:16.120
\h\h\hWaxing 
 When fighting an opponent of higher level, successful criticals reduce your HP, but a power bonus is added to your next attack.

\h\h\hWaning
 When fighting an opponent of higher level, successful criticals restore your HP.

A certain number of successful criticals adds to the fusion gauge.

16:07.110 --> 16:08.590
"Waning—

16:08.590 --> 16:12.280
restores HP under the same circumstances."

16:12.280 --> 16:15.620
Hey, I get it. They really 
do compliment each other!

16:16.040 --> 16:21.080
Eh? "A certain number of successful 
criticals adds to the fusion gauge"?

16:21.360 --> 16:23.520
These weapons freaking combine?!

16:23.520 --> 16:25.380
Gracious, how splendid!

16:25.610 --> 16:27.710
Don't mimic me!

16:29.370 --> 16:31.850
Let's equip these babies 
and give 'em a whirl!

16:33.090 --> 16:35.840
Cannot be wielded due to
failure to meet stat requirements.

16:34.090 --> 16:35.840
Stat requirements?

16:38.270 --> 16:40.350
C-Calm down, dude.

16:40.350 --> 16:53.190
<b>Waxing / Waning</b>

16:40.350 --> 16:53.190
Stat Requirements

16:40.620 --> 16:42.920
It's a simple math problem.

16:42.920 --> 16:46.130
I need 150 stat points in total.

16:46.130 --> 16:49.820
My current total in the relevant stats is 57.

16:50.360 --> 16:53.360
I get five points per level raised, so...

16:53.360 --> 16:56.190
I need to be level 50 to use 'em?!

16:57.640 --> 17:01.830
Well, guess you need to toughen 
up a bit more to use 'em.

17:07.250 --> 17:09.250
S-Sunraku-san?

17:09.460 --> 17:11.500
Sunraku-san?!

17:12.520 --> 17:17.260
But I wanna use them <i>now</i>!

17:17.360 --> 17:20.260
Thirdrema

17:27.270 --> 17:30.770
<b>The Serpent's Apple</b>

17:28.240 --> 17:30.410
So, in conclusion...

17:30.790 --> 17:32.630
I'm late. Sorry!

17:33.000 --> 17:34.780
I really mean it, kinda.

17:38.620 --> 17:41.490
I hope you figured out your last words!

17:41.490 --> 17:44.450
We were supposed to meet 
three damn hours ago!

17:44.450 --> 17:47.420
That's too late to just "sorry" away!

17:47.420 --> 17:51.370
The truth is, I was plugging 
along on a unique scenario,

17:51.370 --> 17:54.170
and Wethermon's name came up...

17:54.390 --> 17:57.280
So I thought it might be worth pursuing.

17:58.550 --> 18:01.220
All right. Spill, and I'll call us even.

18:01.220 --> 18:03.560
Huh? Just scot-free like that?!

18:04.490 --> 18:08.330
Though... that's a bold little 
avatar you got, Katzo.

18:09.190 --> 18:12.690
Actually, I guess you're... Oikatzo here?

18:12.690 --> 18:14.440
Like the soup base, Oigatsuo?

18:14.440 --> 18:17.450
<b><i>Oikatzo</i></b>

18:14.840 --> 18:16.980
{M}He always picks names like that.

18:17.450 --> 18:20.450
<b>Kei Uomi</b>

18:17.450 --> 18:22.720
<b>Modor Katzo</b>

18:17.450 --> 18:22.720
<b>Oikatzo</b>

18:17.450 --> 18:22.720
<b>Katzo Tataki</b>

18:17.680 --> 18:19.950
<i>His real name combines into 
the character "Katsuo,"</i>

18:19.950 --> 18:22.720
<i>so he always sticks "Katzo" in there.</i>

18:20.450 --> 18:22.700
<b>Katsuo (Skipjack Tuna)</b>

18:22.720 --> 18:25.530
I don't need pointers on 
character design from you,

18:25.530 --> 18:29.560
criminal exhibitionist Sunraku-kun.

18:30.520 --> 18:34.380
I'm sure you don't appreciate how 
hard it was for me to get here.

18:34.380 --> 18:38.780
I chose a back-alley place 
with especially low traffic,

18:38.780 --> 18:40.390
so you can relax while you're here.

18:40.770 --> 18:43.300
No wonder it was so hard to find.

18:43.760 --> 18:45.680
Anyway, let's get to brass tacks.

18:46.000 --> 18:48.350
Mind telling me what you learned?

18:49.040 --> 18:49.810
Sure.

18:51.470 --> 18:52.810
I see.

18:52.810 --> 18:59.070
He called Wethermon the Tombguard 
"a living corpse" who'd "outlived his time"?

18:59.890 --> 19:02.200
Are we talking about an undead monster here?

19:02.450 --> 19:07.410
His movements did seem a bit janky 
when the fight first started.

19:08.030 --> 19:09.430
I see.

19:09.430 --> 19:12.080
I'd assumed he was a cyborg-type, but...

19:12.300 --> 19:15.040
Being undead would explain a lot.

19:15.040 --> 19:16.960
Anything there that can help with our strats?

19:20.490 --> 19:23.260
I've got some things to take care of.

19:23.260 --> 19:25.010
Let's split up until nightfall.

19:25.010 --> 19:28.330
Sure, but... what should we do next?

19:28.330 --> 19:30.510
I'll give you guys these for now.

19:30.510 --> 19:34.270
Go grind in the Iron Ruins in the meantime.

19:32.900 --> 19:34.270
Give

19:32.900 --> 19:34.270
Drop

19:34.270 --> 19:35.860
Grind levels, huh?

19:35.860 --> 19:38.810
I'm all for it, but...

19:39.780 --> 19:41.030
A map, and...

19:41.610 --> 19:42.790
...a fishing rod?

19:43.370 --> 19:44.930
It'll make sense when you get there.

19:57.130 --> 20:00.010
I've been wondering since 
you first arrived...

20:00.010 --> 20:04.050
Sunraku-kun, do you actually 
think that disguise is working?

20:04.620 --> 20:08.020
Pray tell? This is merely 
the latest fashion trend...

20:08.560 --> 20:10.810
Huh? What is it?

20:11.410 --> 20:13.590
I guess he fooled one of us?

20:13.590 --> 20:16.530
Maybe if you haven't seen her, 
it doesn't seem off?

20:16.530 --> 20:17.820
Well, whatever.

20:17.820 --> 20:20.650
See you back here tonight.

20:20.650 --> 20:21.420
Sure.

20:21.740 --> 20:23.220
Later.

20:24.060 --> 20:27.200
Okay, let's get down to business!

20:27.200 --> 20:30.190
The Iron Ruins of the Divinity, right?

20:30.190 --> 20:33.900
Hold on while I plan a 
safe route to the gate.

20:35.190 --> 20:36.500
What a pain.

20:36.500 --> 20:38.960
I gotta sneak around now, too, huh?

20:38.960 --> 20:40.960
Sunraku-san! Sunraku-san!

20:40.960 --> 20:43.670
I'm getting a terrible earache!

20:44.360 --> 20:47.220
Might I please move around a bit?

20:57.600 --> 20:58.990
Sunraku!

20:58.990 --> 21:00.770
Your equipment's talking!

21:00.770 --> 21:01.860
It is, isn't it?!

21:02.070 --> 21:03.680
Okay, go on.

21:03.680 --> 21:06.790
I thought it'd be fun to see 
how long it took him to notice.

21:06.790 --> 21:08.200
Indeed...

21:08.200 --> 21:12.150
Is this NPC that unique one?

21:12.150 --> 21:14.050
Can I have a closer look?

21:14.420 --> 21:15.920
What are you doing?!

21:16.230 --> 21:17.590
Unhand me!

21:17.590 --> 21:21.360
Man, I want unique stuff, too!

21:21.690 --> 21:23.920
Let me go, I say!

21:21.920 --> 21:23.520
Get your own, then.

21:26.470 --> 21:29.990
Here we are. The entrance at last!

21:29.990 --> 21:33.450
I want unique stuff too. You lucky dog!

21:33.450 --> 21:36.120
That's all you've been 
saying this whole time.

21:36.120 --> 21:37.650
Let's get going.

21:37.650 --> 21:40.550
I wanna get to level 50 ASAP.

21:40.550 --> 21:41.920
Fine, fine.

21:41.920 --> 21:45.570
But this is my first time in a party in <i>SLF</i>.

21:45.830 --> 21:47.990
My first time with another player, too.

21:50.640 --> 21:53.430
It's got a pretty different vibe 
from the rest of the world so far...

21:53.430 --> 21:55.160
Seems like it could be fun.

21:55.160 --> 21:58.960
Yeah. The Iron Ruins of the Divinity, huh?

22:00.020 --> 22:06.010
Iron Ruins of the Divinity

23:41.980 --> 23:49.240
<b>SLF Mini</b>

23:42.680 --> 23:46.490
<i>SLF</i> Theater!

23:45.790 --> 23:49.240
<i><b>Sunraku's Theme Song</b></i>

23:46.490 --> 23:48.090
Mini!

23:49.240 --> 25:09.320
<i><b>SLF Theater</b></i>

23:49.970 --> 23:54.150
<i>Off fly the sparks</i>

23:54.150 --> 23:59.040
<i>Engulfed by the night</i>

23:59.040 --> 24:03.050
<i>The hammer dances</i>

24:03.050 --> 24:06.960
<i>The iron sings</i>

24:07.920 --> 24:12.180
<i>Bang, clang, ring</i>

24:12.180 --> 24:15.590
<i>Crash, clash, bash</i>

24:15.590 --> 24:20.120
<i>A blade's what you are</i>

24:20.120 --> 24:24.670
<i>Power's what you are</i>

24:25.870 --> 24:27.770
So cool!

24:27.770 --> 24:29.980
What a great song.

24:29.980 --> 24:34.660
Hey, Sunraku-kun, why don't you sing 
your own theme song when you roll in?

24:35.130 --> 24:36.530
Theme song?

24:42.790 --> 24:45.160
<i>Coo, coo, coo</i>

24:45.160 --> 24:47.560
<i>The pigeon goes "coo"</i>

24:47.560 --> 24:51.800
<i>If a pea is what you want, 
I'll give it to you</i>

24:51.800 --> 24:53.300
I'm not a damn pigeon!

24:53.300 --> 24:55.690
But it's a perfect fit for you.

24:55.690 --> 24:57.050
Yeah, totally!

24:57.050 --> 24:58.550
How, exactly?!

25:00.030 --> 25:00.890
Take that!

25:04.750 --> 25:09.320
<b>"Like a pigeon hit with a peashooter" (saying)
 Taken off guard; stunned.
Eyes widened in shock. "Like a peashooter to a pigeon."
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hFrom Kojien, 7th Edition</b>
